---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About — Junwon Lee"
  description="Junwon Lee — MS student at IRIS Lab, Sungkyunkwan University. Training-free acceleration of diffusion LLMs, KV-cache compression, quantization, and efficient inference systems."
  jsonLd={{
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Person',
    name: 'Junwon Lee',
    alternateName: '이준원',
    url: 'https://romaanj.github.io/about/',
    email: 'jwlee1218@g.skku.edu',
    affiliation: {
      '@type': 'Organization',
      name: 'IRIS Lab, Sungkyunkwan University',
      url: 'https://iris.skku.edu/',
    },
    alumniOf: 'Sungkyunkwan University',
    sameAs: [
      'https://github.com/Romaanj',
      'https://www.linkedin.com/in/junwon-lee-961383204/',
      'https://iris.skku.edu/authors/m29_junwon_lee/',
    ],
    knowsAbout: ['diffusion LLMs', 'KV-cache compression', 'quantization', 'efficient inference'],
  }}
>
  <!-- hero -->
  <section class="section hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">About me</p>
        <h1>Hi, I'm Junwon.<br /><em>I make big models run cheap.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">
          MS student at IRIS Lab, Sungkyunkwan University (SKKU), working on
          efficient inference for large models — diffusion LLMs, KV caches,
          quantization, and the stubborn gap between peak FLOPs and the bytes
          a GPU can actually move.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- decorative monogram (no photo, on purpose) -->
      <div class="monogram-wrap" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg class="monogram" viewBox="0 0 240 240" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img">
          <rect x="4" y="4" width="232" height="232" rx="24" class="mg-ground" />
          <!-- quarter-circle, coral -->
          <path d="M 236 236 L 236 140 A 96 96 0 0 0 140 236 Z" class="mg-coral" />
          <!-- small geometric friends -->
          <circle cx="52" cy="188" r="14" class="mg-olive" />
          <path d="M 178 44 L 206 92 L 150 92 Z" class="mg-kraft" />
          <!-- serif initials -->
          <text x="46" y="132" class="mg-letters">JL</text>
          <!-- roofline: bandwidth slope meeting the compute ceiling -->
          <path d="M 46 158 L 118 150 L 194 150" class="mg-roofline" />
        </svg>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- bio -->
  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          My research interest is <strong>training-free acceleration</strong>:
          making inference faster and lighter without touching the weights.
          Right now that means diffusion LLMs — an architecture whose serving
          story is still being written — and the KV-cache machinery around
          them: compression, quantization, and deciding which bytes deserve
          to live in HBM at all.
        </p>
        <p>
          I try to be a measurement-first researcher. Before proposing a
          method I want a profile, a roofline sketch, and a mechanism I can
          point at — otherwise the "speedup" is usually just a benchmark
          artifact wearing a nice name. The best days in the lab are the ones
          where a plot disagrees with my intuition
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- what I care about -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Principles</p>
      <h2>What I care about</h2>
      <div class="card-grid values">
        <div class="card">
          <span class="card-kicker">Bottlenecks</span>
          <h3>The memory wall, not the FLOP count</h3>
          <p>
            Modern accelerators rarely starve for arithmetic — they starve for
            bytes. I read systems through a roofline lens: find where the
            workload actually sits, then attack that ceiling, not the one in
            the marketing slide.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="card-kicker">Constraint</span>
          <h3>Training-free by default</h3>
          <p>
            The most useful acceleration is the kind you can apply to a
            checkpoint this afternoon. No retraining runs, no distillation
            budget — just a sharper use of what the model already computes.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="card-kicker">Discipline</span>
          <h3>Measurement before method</h3>
          <p>
            A method should be the corollary of a mechanism you have actually
            observed. Profile first, form a hypothesis, design the experiment
            that could kill it — then, and only then, write the method section.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="card-kicker">Taste</span>
          <h3>End-to-end honesty</h3>
          <p>
            Speedups are reported wall-clock, end-to-end, at matched quality —
            not in the flattering microbenchmark. If a trick only wins in a
            corner case, the paper should say which corner.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- background -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Background</p>
      <h2>A short timeline</h2>
      <ol class="timeline">
        <li>
          <span class="tl-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="tl-body">
            <span class="tl-when">2026–Present</span>
            <h3>M.S. student — IRIS Lab, Sungkyunkwan University</h3>
            <p>
              Efficient inference for large models: diffusion-LLM acceleration,
              KV-cache compression and quantization, GPU memory systems.
              Advised by Prof. Jong Hwan Ko.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="tl-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="tl-body">
            <span class="tl-when">2020–2026</span>
            <h3>B.S. — Electronic and Electrical Engineering, Sungkyunkwan University</h3>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- contact -->
  <section class="section-tight contact">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="contact-row">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>
          <h2>Say hello</h2>
          <p class="contact-note">
            Happy to talk about efficient inference, diffusion LLMs, or GPU
            systems — 커피챗 환영합니다.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="contact-actions">
          <a class="btn" href="mailto:jwlee1218@g.skku.edu">Email me</a>
          <a class="btn ghost" href="https://github.com/Romaanj" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub — Romaanj</a>
          <a class="btn ghost" href="https://iris.skku.edu/authors/m29_junwon_lee/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">IRIS Lab profile</a>
          <a class="btn ghost" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/junwon-lee-961383204/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>
          <a class="arrow-link" href="/study/">See what I'm studying</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: clamp(3.5rem, 9vw, 7rem); }
  .hero h1 em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--accent-strong);
  }
  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 250px;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    align-items: center;
  }
  .lede { margin-top: 1.6rem; }

  /* monogram */
  .monogram-wrap { justify-self: end; }
  .monogram {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 250px;
  }
  .mg-ground {
    fill: var(--surface-warm);
    stroke: var(--line);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }
  .mg-coral { fill: var(--accent); }
  .mg-olive { fill: var(--swatch-olive); }
  .mg-kraft { fill: var(--swatch-kraft); }
  .mg-letters {
    font-family: 'Source Serif 4 Variable', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 92px;
    font-weight: 600;
    fill: var(--text);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .mg-roofline {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--accent-strong);
    stroke-width: 4;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  /* warm band for values */
  .band-warm {
    background: var(--surface-warm);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .band-warm h2 { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .values .card h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; }

  /* timeline */
  .timeline {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 2.2rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    position: relative;
    max-width: 720px;
  }
  .timeline::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 7px;
    top: 6px;
    bottom: 6px;
    width: 2px;
    background: var(--line);
  }
  .timeline li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0 0 2.2rem 2.2rem;
  }
  .timeline li:last-child { padding-bottom: 0; }
  .tl-dot {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.35rem;
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 3px solid var(--accent);
  }
  .timeline li:first-child .tl-dot { background: var(--accent); }
  .tl-when {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--accent-strong);
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }
  .tl-body h3 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin: 0 0 0.4rem; }
  .tl-body p { color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text) 72%, transparent); max-width: 60ch; }

  /* contact */
  .contact-row {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 2rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }
  .contact-note {
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text) 72%, transparent);
    max-width: 42ch;
  }
  .contact-actions {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .hero-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .monogram-wrap { justify-self: start; }
    .monogram { max-width: 180px; }
  }
</style>
